// fork_point.proto — where a fork of a conversation ends: the vocabulary
// GetForkPoint answers and ForkSession takes.
//
// WHY THE PARENT'S SHIM NAMES IT. A fork carries only FINISHED turns of the
// parent's conversation, so a fork taken while the parent is mid-turn ends just
// before that turn began. Only the shim that drives the parent has seen every
// message of every turn in order — including a turn the vendor started on its
// own — so only it can name the transcript record a finished turn ended on
// without racing the vendor. The daemon relays the point to the CHILD's shim
